# Runtime caches that must never be shipped in a deployment image.
# The .db_name_cache used to persist a discovered MongoDB database name
# across restarts. A stale cached value ("database") once broke production
# by pointing the container at a non-existent DB, so we now detect the
# db name fresh on every boot and explicitly exclude the cache file here
# to prevent it from ever sneaking into a deploy artifact.
backend/.db_name_cache
.db_name_cache
